0038: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0039:     """
0040:     Slide black shapes rightward to a grey separator, then shoot red rays from enclosed holes.
0041: 
0042:     Input structure:
0043:     - A vertical grey (5) separator column divides the grid into left and right halves.
0044:     - Black shapes sit on the left side against a background color (bg).
0045: 
0046:     Rule:
0047:     - Translate each black connected component rightward until its right edge is flush with the separator.
0048:     - After sliding, find enclosed bg regions (holes) within the black shapes that touch the column just left of the separator.
0049:     - For each row spanned by such a hole, emit a red ray across the entire right half of the grid.
0050: 
0051:     Key insight: Only holes adjacent to the separator trigger rays — the sliding creates enclosures that act as "nozzles" projecting rightward.
0052:     """
